                        ],
                        "form": "жу́пеле"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "acda560f-94a4-4b4f-abb2-665237f3e910",
                        "entry_id": "ca87223c-d210-30a6-a8a5-065fa71400a7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "жу́пелах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5dc503d2-6530-35c0-8447-68facf0513ba",
                        "entry_id": "ca87223c-d210-30a6-a8a5-065fa71400a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ. по христианским представлениям, горящая сера, смола для грешников в аду"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "856a75d0-0741-4f2d-a941-e1aa49488ac6",
                                "sense_id": "5dc503d2-6530-35c0-8447-68facf0513ba",
                                "text": "..особенно в законе уголовном должно смотреть, чтобы цель устрашения не обращалась в цель жестокости, и чтоб законы не поражали народ дождём и огня и жупела, о коем говорит Писание.."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d9ef87c-f9e9-4012-aede-f64eb1210ff9",
                                "sense_id": "5dc503d2-6530-35c0-8447-68facf0513ba",
                                "text": "Где огнь и жупел, дым и смрад, // Бессмертный червь не усыпает, // Ужасным пламенем рыгает, // Разверзши зёв, свирепый ад"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ce8dc28-3f6a-31f8-a951-f5828a48f40f",
                        "entry_id": "ca87223c-d210-30a6-a8a5-065fa71400a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. то, что внушает страх, ужас, отвращение, чем запугивают кого-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08eaf7b4-718a-41fc-8333-6493628e2916",
                                "sense_id": "3ce8dc28-3f6a-31f8-a951-f5828a48f40f",
                                "text": "Социализм всегда был жупелом для мещан"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3cfafcd-3584-4b41-b6ce-b85a544dc3e5",
                                "sense_id": "3ce8dc28-3f6a-31f8-a951-f5828a48f40f",
                                "text": "А ведь захватили этот дом как раз при том строе, из которого сделали истинно мировой жупел."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "814a20c3-7b5f-4869-934a-f6e8f836c907",
                                "sense_id": "3ce8dc28-3f6a-31f8-a951-f5828a48f40f",
                                "text": "Еврей, да ещё вооружённый университетским дипломом, каждой воинской части казался жупелом, предполагаемым носителем революционной заразы, которого из элементарной осторожности лучше и не подпускать близко к казарме."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7cf32ac6-fa69-4587-85a1-8a7dadc83764",
                        "source_entry_id": "ca87223c-d210-30a6-a8a5-065fa71400a7",
                        "source_sense_description": "горящая сера для грешников",
                        "target_lang_word": "brimstone",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brimstone",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sulfur of hell; hell, damnation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cbf9420-2211-46cd-9e44-22081eca81fa",
                                                "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                                "text": "For griefe thereof, and diuelish despight, / From his infernall fournace forth he threw / Huge flames, that dimmed all the heauens light, / Enrold in duskish smoke and brimstone blew."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d4c525f-ffa0-43e0-9e3c-0b9af1f76872",
                                                "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                                "text": "And thus I sawe the horses in the vision, and them that sate on them, hauing brest-plates of fire and of Iacinct, and brimstone, & the heades of the horses were as the heads of Lions, and out of their mouthes issued fire, and smoke, and brimstone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cbec199-5a40-43ab-9e89-e075caece4d6",
                                                "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                                "text": "Till, as a signal giv'n, th' uplifted Spear / Of their great Sultan waving to direct / Thir course, in even ballance down they light / On the firm brimstone, and fill all the Plain; / A multitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7e42536-0879-4fba-8668-9103dd73ac63",
                                                "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                                "text": "[W]hen he [the Devil] is aweary of vice, and aweary of virtue, used up as to brimstone, and used up as to bliss […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d1e7c8f-68b7-411f-9859-da85fe0f8d02",
                                                "sense_id": "e7499497-4b3b-3c6e-9cdc-439dd5212fed",
                                                "text": "But the sulphurous brimstone which burns in hell is a substance which is specially designed to burn for ever and for ever with unspeakable fury."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ccf6163-a36b-324d-9b54-3c834f0c4173",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sulfur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f145ef9-38fd-4856-9871-a5f3ee2b2909",
                                                "sense_id": "6ccf6163-a36b-324d-9b54-3c834f0c4173",
                                                "text": "Weel I wot I wad be broken if I were to gie sic weight to the folk that come to buy our pepper and brimstone, and suchlike sweetmeats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89fd4fb1-e613-42c5-8505-7ac5bc51a3a4",
                                                "sense_id": "6ccf6163-a36b-324d-9b54-3c834f0c4173",
                                                "text": "Don't think, young man, that we go to the expense of flower of brimstone and molasses, just to purify them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd952a6f-3fe6-3e3f-92b4-46c56799b3fb",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A whore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af056764-371f-44de-bd78-307aec01406b",
                                                "sense_id": "dd952a6f-3fe6-3e3f-92b4-46c56799b3fb",
                                                "text": "I went to the park, picked up a low Brimstone, called myself a Barber, & agreed with her for Sixpence, went to the bottom of the park, arm in arm, & dipped my machine in the Canal […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "532185ab-5f95-3c93-95cc-e08a37c63569",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used attributively as an intensifier in exclamations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0b55edc-cc40-4457-b785-58b24b9cafba",
                                                "sense_id": "532185ab-5f95-3c93-95cc-e08a37c63569",
                                                "text": "You are a brimstone pig. You're a head of swine!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7957b97-6bfc-448f-968c-1ddd6d144f00",
                                                "sense_id": "532185ab-5f95-3c93-95cc-e08a37c63569",
                                                "text": "You're a brimstone idiot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c94407e5-2d85-4ecd-b10c-dc0da58d1425",
                                                "sense_id": "532185ab-5f95-3c93-95cc-e08a37c63569",
                                                "text": "I made a speaking trumpet of my hands and commenced to whoop “Ahoy!” and “Hello!” at the top of my lungs. […] The Colonel woke up, and, after asking what in brimstone was the matter, opened his mouth and roared “Hi!” and “Hello!” like the bull of Bashan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93f80d9e-15fc-3d1b-a29a-26f4b2c5efdf",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The butterfly Gonepteryx rhamni of the Pieridae family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7962a782-6bed-3d45-8dc1-23174085687c",
                                        "entry_id": "6fe38c85-c16e-3070-8279-4a74d2dc83c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Online content of exceptionally poor quality, lower than coal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet",
